From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:56:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/ane: h16: let the ANE DARTs suspend once the
 device is bound

The H16 backend powers its five domains and three DARTs with explicit
votes and never enables runtime PM on the ANE device, so the
DL_FLAG_RPM_ACTIVE vote the IOMMU core left on each DART was never
released. On the T8132, which stops after the preload identity and takes
no vote of its own, the three ANE DARTs stayed runtime-active and held
ane_sys on at idle while the other ANE domains were off.

Hand the link votes back at the end of probe with
ane_pm_drop_link_votes(). The device stays bound and identified, the
start work and the debugfs stages are unchanged, and when the engine is
powered ane_h16_acquire() still votes for the DARTs itself.

Fixes: e40b1e936d1b ("accel/ane: sync the ANE driver with aurora integration/aurora")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c
index a89bab0f3e..236d3ab3e2 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 #include "ane_h16_accel.h"
 #include "ane_h16_boot.h"
 #include "ane_h16_preload.h"
+#include "ane_pm.h"
 
 #define ANE_H16_TX_WORDS 272
 /* Private program window above the SHAREDMALLOC range; host policy. */
@@ -1879,6 +1880,15 @@ int ane_h16_backend_probe(struct platform_device *pdev, const struct ane_fw_plat
 	debugfs_create_u64("irq_wakeups", 0400, h->debugfs, &h->irq_wakeups);
 	debugfs_create_u64("irq_timeouts", 0400, h->debugfs, &h->irq_timeouts);
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, h);
+	/*
+	 * The IOMMU core left one runtime-PM vote on each DART for this device
+	 * (DL_FLAG_RPM_ACTIVE links), held until the device first suspends. The
+	 * backend votes for its DARTs and domains itself, so hand those back:
+	 * otherwise the DARTs keep ane_sys on for as long as the device is bound.
+	 */
+	ret = ane_pm_drop_link_votes(h->dev);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(h->dev, "H16 DART link votes kept, error %d; ane_sys stays on\n", ret);
 	INIT_WORK(&h->start, ane_h16_start_work);
 	schedule_work(&h->start);
 	ret = 0;
